{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqei0h7cyxc","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"daemon native task ingestion should auto-wire blockedBy into orchestrator graph blocking edges","summary":"Gap: when the daemon ingests native task files (~/.claude/tasks/<session>/<id>.json), it reads subject/status/description but does NOT parse the blockedBy field. So native task dependencies never become orchestrator graph blocking edges — they have to be wired manually via add_dependency, causing double-wiring friction and footguns (tasks appear ready in the graph when they shouldn't be). Fix: in the native task ingestion path, when a task file has blockedBy: [\"3\"], look up the sibling key (<session>/3) and emit a blocking edge into the overlay automatically. This makes TaskUpdate(addBlockedBy) sufficient — no separate add_dependency call needed.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T00:52:12.696Z","vec":[-0.09575188905000687,0.008682391606271267,0.016953855752944946,-0.03376096487045288,0.032062333077192307,-0.023626990616321564,-0.003104437841102481,0.008835885673761368,-0.04826325178146362,0.053597770631313324,-0.04902355745434761,-0.023319676518440247,-0.08234833925962448,0.011979351751506329,0.05088130012154579,0.026676533743739128,0.13192041218280792,-0.10241430252790451,0.03789009153842926,-0.0546516589820385,-0.0067308456636965275,-0.017091529443860054,0.021688509732484818,0.016304751858115196,-0.03610239177942276,0.008230393752455711,-0.07740253955125809,-0.05816616863012314,0.043006908148527145,0.013257430866360664,0.013594371266663074,0.039081722497940063,-0.0583793930709362,0.042093418538570404,0.026627419516444206,0.07346158474683762,-0.00005644045086228289,-0.015954118221998215,-0.07361161708831787,0.026100818067789078,0.05006856471300125,0.06485588848590851,-0.02388712391257286,-0.04169682413339615,-0.03536786139011383,-0.06424769759178162,-0.11298897862434387,-0.05776119977235794,-0.052519142627716064,0.002241534413769841,-0.0359318777918815